    "body": "### Description\n\nI have a usecase where i need to extend the middleware and use request.path\n\n`class CustomCorsMiddleware(CorsMiddleware):\n    def origin_found_in_white_lists(self, origin: str, url: SplitResult) -> bool:\n        request = self.request\n\n        if \"/sdk/\" in request.path:\n            return True\n\n        return super().origin_found_in_white_lists(origin, url)\n`\n\nbut in the main method, `add_response_headers` where `origin_found_in_white_lists` is called, request is not passed. Are we able to do that ?",
