    "body": "### Understanding CORS\n\n- [x] I have read the resources.\n\n### Python Version\n\n3.12\n\n### Django Version\n\n6.0.3\n\n### Package Version\n\n4.9.0\n\n### Description\n\nModern browsers (Chrome 124+, Safari, etc.) now automatically include the `priority` header (RFC 9218) in fetch() requests to signal resource urgency.\n\nBecause this header is not CORS-safelisted, it triggers a preflight request. If `priority` is not explicitly added to `CORS_ALLOW_HEADERS`, the request fails with a CORS error. Adding this to the default list would align the package with current browser behaviors and prevent \"out-of-the-box\" failures for standard fetch calls.\n\nhttps://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/HTTP/Headers/Priority",
